 "description": "Measured the temporal stage on the 4K fixture (desktop -O2,\n261110_004208_VIDEO_24mm.mcraw, 3840x2160 RGGB, 310 frames, both\nneighbors, real noise profiles) with a throwaway probe under\nbuild/desktop (gitignored, like probe_shift.cpp).\n\nPer-stage (TemporalReport, strength 100): proxy 0.8-2.2 ms,\nmatch 7.9-12.1 ms, merge 76.7-93.1 ms; total ~85-107 ms per\nframe. Strength 50 lands in the same band. The merge is a\nfull-res per-pixel stage that runs BEFORE the develop tail, so\nmaxDim does not shrink it: develop at 720px is 6.1-6.5 ms and\nat 1280px 23.7-26.5 ms, but the temporal cost is identical at\nevery tier.\n\nSteady-state sequential playback with the capacity-4 ring\n(probe walk of frames 147..163, strength 100): 19 decodes over\n17 steps = 1.12 decodes/frame — the ring amortizes to ~1 decode\nper rendered frame as designed; decode 4.9-5.2 ms/step, merge\n76.7-83.8 ms/step, develop720 6.1-6.3 ",
